1
00:00:06,065 --> 00:00:08,224
<i>I've never had feelings for you.</i>

2
00:00:08,305 --> 00:00:09,465
<i>Never.</i>

3
00:00:09,545 --> 00:00:13,105
And no matter how hard you try,
I'll never fall for you.

4
00:00:13,185 --> 00:00:15,305
<i>You can make things easier on yourself.</i>

5
00:00:15,385 --> 00:00:19,025
You just need to choose your own
peace of mind first.

6
00:00:19,105 --> 00:00:21,265
<i>Love is really about courage.</i>

7
00:00:22,265 --> 00:00:23,345
What about you?

8
00:00:23,425 --> 00:00:24,625
Why not be brave for once?

9
00:00:24,705 --> 00:00:27,785
<i>But if you think</i>
<i>what I did means that much,</i>

10
00:00:27,865 --> 00:00:29,585
<i>then I'd like something in return.</i>

11
00:00:29,665 --> 00:00:31,305
Stay away from my granddaughter.

12
00:00:31,385 --> 00:00:33,545
<i>I'll disappear from Piang's life.</i>

13
00:00:34,945 --> 00:00:36,985
I'll be the one to leave.

14
00:00:42,905 --> 00:00:43,865
Where are you going?

15
00:00:56,625 --> 00:00:58,185
That's my business.

16
00:00:58,905 --> 00:01:00,425
You don't need to interfere, Grandma.

17
00:01:00,505 --> 00:01:01,545
Piang.

18
00:01:03,345 --> 00:01:05,865
You've never spoken
to me like this before.

19
00:01:06,425 --> 00:01:09,025
Has this woman really
changed you that much?

20
00:01:11,145 --> 00:01:13,385
It has nothing to do with Song.

21
00:01:13,465 --> 00:01:15,585
It's because of you.

22
00:01:18,545 --> 00:01:20,785
The last time you talked to her,

23
00:01:20,865 --> 00:01:22,745
I let it slide.

24
00:01:23,665 --> 00:01:25,625
But you're doing it again.

25
00:01:26,785 --> 00:01:27,905
Why?

26
00:01:27,985 --> 00:01:30,505
Just because she's not right for me?

27
00:01:30,585 --> 00:01:32,345
-Is that all?
-Yes.

28
00:01:33,185 --> 00:01:35,225
Because compatibility matters.

29
00:01:37,265 --> 00:01:39,825
As long as this woman stays in your life,

30
00:01:39,905 --> 00:01:42,025
you'll keep chasing after her.

31
00:01:42,105 --> 00:01:44,065
Have some self-respect.

32
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:48,105
I raised you,
not to make yourself look so pathetic.

33
00:01:49,425 --> 00:01:50,865
I don't care.

34
00:01:51,665 --> 00:01:55,425
Even if I have to keep chasing her
until I'm exhausted, I'll do it.

35
00:01:58,505 --> 00:02:01,185
Because love means everything to me.

36
00:02:01,265 --> 00:02:02,465
Piangrawin.

37
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:09,905
Grandma.

38
00:02:10,785 --> 00:02:14,825
All my life,
I've done everything you've asked.

39
00:02:16,785 --> 00:02:21,105
Can I ask for just this one thing?
To follow my heart for once.

40
00:02:23,705 --> 00:02:25,585
But if in the end,

41
00:02:26,185 --> 00:02:28,385
Song doesn't return my feelings,

42
00:02:29,465 --> 00:02:30,865
I'll accept it.

43
00:02:31,385 --> 00:02:34,025
And whatever you want me to do,

44
00:02:34,105 --> 00:02:36,505
I'll do exactly as you say.

45
00:02:52,545 --> 00:02:53,705
No.

46
00:03:14,665 --> 00:03:15,905
Okay.

47
00:03:17,825 --> 00:03:20,305
Then I guess I made the right decision.

48
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:26,225
I'm leaving you.

49
00:03:26,305 --> 00:03:27,905
And I won't come back.

50
00:03:41,945 --> 00:03:45,665
Do you see how much
of a problem you are now?

51
00:05:20,305 --> 00:05:21,905
Song, are you okay?

52
00:05:21,985 --> 00:05:23,185
Just look at her.

53
00:05:23,265 --> 00:05:24,585
With that look on her face,

54
00:05:24,665 --> 00:05:26,345
something must've happened again, right?

55
00:05:27,865 --> 00:05:28,905
Song.

56
00:05:30,625 --> 00:05:32,065
Where are Grandma and Piang?

57
00:05:38,505 --> 00:05:39,865
Did something happen?

58
00:05:57,585 --> 00:05:59,825
You know everything already, don't you?

59
00:06:11,545 --> 00:06:12,785
Piang.

60
00:06:14,185 --> 00:06:15,945
Piang, please open the door.

61
00:06:48,305 --> 00:06:50,585
PIANG

62
00:07:14,585 --> 00:07:15,585
Hello, Song.

63
00:07:16,265 --> 00:07:18,345
<i>Piang has disappeared.</i>

64
00:07:18,425 --> 00:07:19,705
<i>She's not picking up my calls.</i>

65
00:07:20,305 --> 00:07:23,705
Do you happen to know
where Piang might have gone?

66
00:07:23,785 --> 00:07:24,785
I have no idea.

67
00:07:24,865 --> 00:07:27,105
Other than home,
she has nowhere else to go.

68
00:07:29,545 --> 00:07:31,345
I'm sorry.

69
00:07:31,425 --> 00:07:34,585
I'm partly responsible for her decision.

70
00:07:34,665 --> 00:07:37,145
This isn't the time to blame yourself.

71
00:07:37,225 --> 00:07:40,025
Right now, we need to find Piang.

72
00:07:40,105 --> 00:07:41,985
I'll call Mon, her best friend.

73
00:07:42,065 --> 00:07:44,625
Could you help keep calling Piang too?

74
00:07:44,705 --> 00:07:46,105
<i>Of course.</i>

75
00:07:46,185 --> 00:07:47,425
Thank you.

76
00:07:54,465 --> 00:07:56,505
PIANG

77
00:08:24,025 --> 00:08:24,985
Hello, Mon.

78
00:08:25,065 --> 00:08:26,545
Are you with Piang?

79
00:08:26,625 --> 00:08:27,585
<i>No, Mudmee.</i>

80
00:08:27,665 --> 00:08:29,465
<i>I'm in Australia for work right now.</i>

81
00:08:30,265 --> 00:08:31,425
Okay.

82
00:08:32,585 --> 00:08:33,625
Just let her go.

83
00:08:43,664 --> 00:08:46,065
I'd like to see for myself

84
00:08:46,145 --> 00:08:48,265
how long your sister
can manage on her own.

85
00:08:48,345 --> 00:08:50,425
-But Grandma…
-That's an order.

86
00:08:51,705 --> 00:08:53,945
If you disobey me, you'll regret it.

87
00:08:54,025 --> 00:08:56,145
And if something happens to her,

88
00:08:56,225 --> 00:08:58,065
won't you regret it?

89
00:08:58,145 --> 00:09:00,345
If you're not bringing her back,

90
00:09:00,425 --> 00:09:02,985
at least we should know where she is.

91
00:09:43,065 --> 00:09:45,825
Send someone
to keep an eye on Piang for me.

92
00:09:48,545 --> 00:09:49,865
No need.

93
00:09:52,145 --> 00:09:54,705
Do exactly as I said.

94
00:09:55,345 --> 00:09:56,505
Understood?

95
00:10:01,345 --> 00:10:02,305
I'm sorry,

96
00:10:02,985 --> 00:10:05,025
but your credit card was declined.

97
00:10:05,105 --> 00:10:06,545
What?

98
00:10:11,865 --> 00:10:13,265
Grandma.

99
00:10:13,945 --> 00:10:16,185
How would you like to pay, Ma'am?

100
00:10:17,225 --> 00:10:19,745
-Could I see the bill again?
-Of course.

101
00:10:22,265 --> 00:10:23,865
TOTAL 14,053 BAHT

102
00:10:27,465 --> 00:10:29,785
BALANCE 1,180.20 BAHT

103
00:10:39,265 --> 00:10:41,905
I'm sorry, but could I pay later?

104
00:10:41,985 --> 00:10:43,345
I'm short on cash.

105
00:10:43,425 --> 00:10:45,465
I'll bring the money tomorrow.

106
00:10:45,545 --> 00:10:46,385
I'm afraid not.

107
00:10:46,465 --> 00:10:48,665
That's not our policy.

108
00:10:48,745 --> 00:10:50,065
Mobile payment works too.

109
00:10:51,225 --> 00:10:53,625
My bank account has a problem too.

110
00:10:53,705 --> 00:10:56,345
Please trust me,
I'll pay you back tomorrow.

111
00:10:59,025 --> 00:11:00,225
Here.

112
00:11:01,425 --> 00:11:02,985
I'm Piang Piangrawin Chatpimuk,

113
00:11:03,065 --> 00:11:05,265
the granddaughter of
the owner of One Two Six Food.

114
00:11:05,345 --> 00:11:07,585
I'm not trying to dine and dash.

115
00:11:12,305 --> 00:11:15,145
Are you… laughing at me?

116
00:11:18,825 --> 00:11:21,105
It doesn't matter who you are.

117
00:11:21,185 --> 00:11:22,105
If you don't pay,

118
00:11:22,185 --> 00:11:23,905
you can't leave this restaurant.

119
00:11:23,985 --> 00:11:25,305
Come on, I already told you.

120
00:11:25,385 --> 00:11:26,665
I don't have enough money.

121
00:11:26,745 --> 00:11:28,105
I'll pay you back.

122
00:11:28,185 --> 00:11:31,105
If you don't settle the bill now,

123
00:11:31,185 --> 00:11:34,145
we'll have to call the police.

124
00:11:36,825 --> 00:11:39,425
-Please trust me. But…
-Hey.

125
00:11:39,505 --> 00:11:41,505
Don't make this a bigger issue than it is.

126
00:11:41,585 --> 00:11:43,985
I'll pay for her.

127
00:11:44,585 --> 00:11:45,825
Certainly, Your Highness.

128
00:11:50,025 --> 00:11:51,585
Thank you, um…

129
00:11:53,265 --> 00:11:55,025
Thank you, Your Highness.

130
00:11:55,105 --> 00:11:57,225
You don't have to call me Your Highness.

131
00:11:57,305 --> 00:12:01,265
You can call me Grandma or Granny.

132
00:12:02,425 --> 00:12:03,825
Yes, Grandma.

133
00:12:06,065 --> 00:12:09,025
May I have your phone number?

134
00:12:09,105 --> 00:12:12,065
Once I have the money,
I'll pay you back right away.

135
00:12:12,145 --> 00:12:14,225
You don't need to pay me back.

136
00:12:14,305 --> 00:12:16,425
Just sit and have a drink with me.

137
00:12:17,945 --> 00:12:18,905
Huh?

138
00:12:22,305 --> 00:12:23,625
But…

139
00:12:24,745 --> 00:12:26,385
It's 14,000 baht.

140
00:12:28,545 --> 00:12:30,025
Don't worry about it.

141
00:12:34,225 --> 00:12:35,625
Your name is Piang, right?

142
00:12:36,865 --> 00:12:37,945
Yes.

143
00:12:38,585 --> 00:12:41,625
Are you having some trouble? Huh?

144
00:12:41,705 --> 00:12:43,385
You can tell me about it.

145
00:12:43,465 --> 00:12:45,385
I have a granddaughter too.

146
00:12:45,465 --> 00:12:48,745
She's about your age,
a Gen Z just like you.

147
00:12:55,345 --> 00:12:58,545
Well… I had a fight with my grandma.

148
00:13:01,105 --> 00:13:03,425
She tries to control
everything in my life,

149
00:13:03,505 --> 00:13:05,225
even my love life.

150
00:13:08,065 --> 00:13:11,385
But I wouldn't listen to her,
so I ran away from home.

151
00:13:12,505 --> 00:13:16,865
And I only brought a little cash
and my credit card.

152
00:13:16,945 --> 00:13:20,145
But my grandma has already
cut off my credit card.

153
00:13:21,465 --> 00:13:24,825
She probably wants me to give up

154
00:13:24,905 --> 00:13:26,545
and surrender to her.

155
00:13:28,385 --> 00:13:32,945
I never imagined
my grandma could be this cruel.

156
00:13:34,345 --> 00:13:35,985
Do you believe

157
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:39,145
she's probably laughing at me right now?

158
00:13:39,945 --> 00:13:42,145
No, Piang.

159
00:13:42,225 --> 00:13:45,785
I think your grandma

160
00:13:45,865 --> 00:13:48,745
is hurting just as much as you are.

161
00:13:49,665 --> 00:13:52,625
Then why won't she give in for once?

162
00:13:52,705 --> 00:13:54,945
Why does she have to control everything?

163
00:13:56,305 --> 00:13:59,225
Piang, let me ask you something.

164
00:13:59,305 --> 00:14:01,185
Your grandma

165
00:14:01,265 --> 00:14:04,265
raised you since you were little,
didn't she?

166
00:14:05,825 --> 00:14:07,065
Yes.

167
00:14:08,145 --> 00:14:11,705
My parents passed away when I was young.

168
00:14:14,385 --> 00:14:17,225
Then it's not hard to understand.

169
00:14:17,305 --> 00:14:18,585
Listen to me.

170
00:14:18,665 --> 00:14:20,745
Everything

171
00:14:20,825 --> 00:14:22,185
you've told me,

172
00:14:22,265 --> 00:14:24,625
all comes from your grandmother's love

173
00:14:24,705 --> 00:14:26,185
for you.

174
00:14:26,265 --> 00:14:30,625
Sure, she may express it through control.

175
00:14:30,705 --> 00:14:36,105
But that control comes from
your grandmother's love.

176
00:14:37,985 --> 00:14:39,065
How about this?

177
00:14:39,145 --> 00:14:40,745
To sum it up,

178
00:14:40,825 --> 00:14:45,545
my advice is…

179
00:14:45,625 --> 00:14:46,905
What is it?

180
00:14:46,985 --> 00:14:48,025
It's…

181
00:14:48,105 --> 00:14:49,425
What is it?

182
00:14:49,505 --> 00:14:50,425
Nothing.

183
00:14:52,465 --> 00:14:54,985
I'm just teasing you.

184
00:14:56,025 --> 00:14:58,705
Piang, take a guess.

185
00:14:58,785 --> 00:15:01,465
What do you think

186
00:15:01,545 --> 00:15:03,985
my advice will be?

187
00:15:08,545 --> 00:15:11,705
You'll tell me to go talk
to my grandma, right?

188
00:15:13,425 --> 00:15:14,585
Huh?

189
00:15:15,825 --> 00:15:18,545
I think you should stay just as you are.

190
00:15:19,145 --> 00:15:23,145
Because I feel that in some situations,

191
00:15:23,225 --> 00:15:26,705
it's the adults who need to learn,

192
00:15:26,785 --> 00:15:28,225
not the children.

193
00:15:30,465 --> 00:15:32,865
And when will adults learn?

194
00:15:32,945 --> 00:15:34,785
Oh! I don't know that either.

195
00:15:34,865 --> 00:15:39,025
But I can assure you
that day will come eventually.

196
00:15:39,865 --> 00:15:42,025
But right now,

197
00:15:42,105 --> 00:15:44,065
you need to give me
your bank account number.

198
00:15:44,145 --> 00:15:46,065
-I'll transfer some money to you.
-No, thank you.

199
00:15:46,145 --> 00:15:48,585
-Your credit card doesn't work anymore.
-Grandma, I can't accept that.

200
00:15:48,665 --> 00:15:50,785
You don't have to feel bad.

201
00:15:50,865 --> 00:15:56,065
Please don't turn down my kindness.
I want to help.

202
00:15:56,145 --> 00:15:58,785
When you have the money,
you can pay me back.

203
00:15:58,865 --> 00:16:00,785
Most importantly,

204
00:16:00,865 --> 00:16:04,265
I know you wouldn't cheat me.

205
00:16:04,985 --> 00:16:05,945
Right?

206
00:16:07,265 --> 00:16:08,465
Come on.

207
00:16:37,065 --> 00:16:38,545
<i>Thank you, um…</i>

208
00:16:39,305 --> 00:16:41,105
<i>Thank you, Your Highness.</i>

209
00:16:52,465 --> 00:16:54,585
Get me M.R. Salika's phone number.

210
00:17:29,345 --> 00:17:31,345
I'm leaving you, Grandma.

211
00:17:31,425 --> 00:17:33,545
<i>And I'm never coming back.</i>

212
00:17:42,545 --> 00:17:44,665
<i>Show yourself right now.</i>

213
00:17:44,745 --> 00:17:46,745
<i>I thought you said you liked me.</i>

214
00:18:47,425 --> 00:18:48,425
Please.

215
00:18:55,345 --> 00:18:58,665
Thank you for accepting my invitation.

216
00:18:58,745 --> 00:19:00,225
My pleasure.

217
00:19:01,385 --> 00:19:03,625
Then I'll get straight to the point.

218
00:19:11,385 --> 00:19:14,705
This young woman is my granddaughter.

219
00:19:15,345 --> 00:19:17,265
I know.

220
00:19:18,625 --> 00:19:19,585
You know,

221
00:19:21,705 --> 00:19:22,745
yet you still got involved?

222
00:19:22,825 --> 00:19:24,705
I wasn't planning to.

223
00:19:25,305 --> 00:19:29,105
But the girl clearly needed help.

224
00:19:29,185 --> 00:19:31,785
But she's my granddaughter.

225
00:19:31,865 --> 00:19:33,825
I'm the one who
should handle this, not you.

226
00:19:35,145 --> 00:19:36,745
So you're saying I butted in?

227
00:19:38,105 --> 00:19:38,985
Goodness.

228
00:19:39,065 --> 00:19:40,185
Now then,

229
00:19:40,865 --> 00:19:43,745
you're an M.R.,

230
00:19:43,825 --> 00:19:45,865
how can you speak like that?

231
00:19:45,945 --> 00:19:48,185
Speak like what? "Butted in."

232
00:19:49,185 --> 00:19:51,865
It's a perfectly good Thai word,

233
00:19:51,945 --> 00:19:53,985
everyone says it.

234
00:19:54,065 --> 00:19:56,145
And another thing,

235
00:19:56,225 --> 00:19:59,505
an M.R. is still a human being.

236
00:19:59,585 --> 00:20:03,345
-We all eat, poop, have sex, and pee.
-That's enough.

237
00:20:07,745 --> 00:20:08,945
Let's talk about something else.

238
00:20:09,985 --> 00:20:11,425
Anyway,

239
00:20:12,385 --> 00:20:15,145
I'm asking you, from now on,

240
00:20:15,225 --> 00:20:17,785
please stay out of
my granddaughter's life.

241
00:20:20,105 --> 00:20:21,345
Ma'am,

242
00:20:21,425 --> 00:20:23,105
I know very well

243
00:20:23,185 --> 00:20:26,705
that you love your granddaughter dearly.

244
00:20:26,785 --> 00:20:29,305
That's why I also know

245
00:20:29,385 --> 00:20:31,665
that whatever you give her,

246
00:20:31,745 --> 00:20:34,465
you believe it to be

247
00:20:34,545 --> 00:20:36,305
the very best choice.

248
00:20:37,465 --> 00:20:38,665
But don't forget,

249
00:20:38,745 --> 00:20:40,505
your granddaughter

250
00:20:40,585 --> 00:20:43,065
is already an adult.

251
00:20:43,145 --> 00:20:45,425
If you keep interfering

252
00:20:45,505 --> 00:20:48,305
and controlling her life like this,

253
00:20:48,385 --> 00:20:49,665
then what happens

254
00:20:49,745 --> 00:20:51,625
when one day you're gone?

255
00:20:51,705 --> 00:20:55,065
How will your granddaughter live on?

256
00:20:55,145 --> 00:20:57,025
Are you cursing me?

257
00:20:58,385 --> 00:21:00,465
Why would you think that?

258
00:21:00,545 --> 00:21:03,425
Or do you think you're immortal?

259
00:21:03,505 --> 00:21:04,865
So dramatic.

260
00:21:04,945 --> 00:21:08,585
Seriously, what drama have you
been watching lately?

261
00:21:12,265 --> 00:21:14,625
-Are you finished?
-Let's say I am.

262
00:21:18,345 --> 00:21:20,625
Then let me make this clear again.

263
00:21:22,985 --> 00:21:24,945
Stay away from my granddaughter.

264
00:21:25,025 --> 00:21:27,345
And stay away from me too.

265
00:21:27,425 --> 00:21:29,745
It's a simple request.

266
00:21:29,825 --> 00:21:31,345
For someone as smart as you,

267
00:21:31,425 --> 00:21:33,585
I hope you understand.

268
00:21:42,665 --> 00:21:45,185
Such a boomer.

269
00:21:47,305 --> 00:21:49,665
Oh, Piang.

270
00:21:50,705 --> 00:21:53,545
I wish you the best of luck.

271
00:22:05,465 --> 00:22:06,545
Song.

272
00:22:07,745 --> 00:22:08,945
Ple.

273
00:22:09,025 --> 00:22:11,465
What are you doing here?
Are you here to see Ploy?

274
00:22:12,065 --> 00:22:13,665
I'm here to see you.

275
00:22:13,745 --> 00:22:16,145
Ploy told me you're not doing okay.

276
00:22:22,225 --> 00:22:24,465
You're really worried
about Piang, aren't you?

277
00:22:28,905 --> 00:22:30,865
I'm your friend.

278
00:22:30,945 --> 00:22:32,465
You don't have to pretend with me.

279
00:22:34,985 --> 00:22:37,305
Yeah. I admit it.

280
00:22:37,385 --> 00:22:39,065
I'm worried about her.

281
00:22:40,625 --> 00:22:41,905
And the reason you're worried…

282
00:22:43,945 --> 00:22:46,225
is it because you're starting to love her?

283
00:22:50,985 --> 00:22:53,345
I think you should tell her

284
00:22:53,425 --> 00:22:54,745
how you feel.

285
00:22:59,865 --> 00:23:01,265
You know

286
00:23:01,345 --> 00:23:02,945
I can't do that.

287
00:23:03,985 --> 00:23:07,305
Honestly, besides telling
her how you feel,

288
00:23:08,505 --> 00:23:11,345
you should also tell her

289
00:23:12,905 --> 00:23:14,865
what happened eight years ago.

290
00:23:22,105 --> 00:23:25,265
Just tell her.
She'll understand you better.

291
00:23:26,225 --> 00:23:28,345
She'll know you never
meant to push her away.

292
00:23:28,425 --> 00:23:30,665
What you did

293
00:23:31,305 --> 00:23:34,225
was because you have your reasons.

294
00:23:37,185 --> 00:23:39,185
Now isn't the time.

295
00:23:39,265 --> 00:23:41,305
Then when will you tell her?

296
00:23:46,745 --> 00:23:47,785
Song, seriously,

297
00:23:47,865 --> 00:23:50,385
you know the real problem
isn't her grandmother.

298
00:23:50,465 --> 00:23:53,145
If her grandmother knew
whose granddaughter you are,

299
00:23:53,225 --> 00:23:54,585
she'd be fine with it.

300
00:23:57,945 --> 00:24:00,105
The real problem is you.

301
00:24:01,145 --> 00:24:03,945
That's why Piang keeps chasing after you.

302
00:24:07,785 --> 00:24:09,945
Her grandmother already disliked you,

303
00:24:10,025 --> 00:24:12,025
and now she dislikes you even more.

304
00:24:12,745 --> 00:24:16,865
So she tried to stop your relationship
and drove Piang away.

305
00:24:18,225 --> 00:24:19,865
The problem is…

306
00:24:20,905 --> 00:24:24,025
You refuse to move on from your past.

307
00:24:27,985 --> 00:24:30,225
And if the problem starts with you,

308
00:24:32,945 --> 00:24:35,225
then you're the one who has to fix it.

309
00:24:42,105 --> 00:24:43,345
Let me ask you something.

310
00:24:45,225 --> 00:24:46,625
Were you happy

311
00:24:50,465 --> 00:24:52,265
when you found out
Ploy and I were together?

312
00:24:53,305 --> 00:24:54,545
Of course I was.

313
00:24:57,105 --> 00:24:58,905
I'll feel the same way

314
00:24:59,585 --> 00:25:01,665
if things work out between you and Piang.

315
00:25:05,425 --> 00:25:07,025
The two of us

316
00:25:08,465 --> 00:25:10,625
have both been running from love.

317
00:25:13,585 --> 00:25:15,865
If I can start over,

318
00:25:18,265 --> 00:25:19,745
so can you.

319
00:25:40,145 --> 00:25:42,905
MISSED CALL

320
00:26:20,865 --> 00:26:22,705
<i>Song! Song!</i>

321
00:26:22,785 --> 00:26:24,185
Piang just posted an IG story.

322
00:26:24,265 --> 00:26:25,265
Let me see.

323
00:26:32,145 --> 00:26:33,225
This place is…

324
00:26:34,345 --> 00:26:35,625
-Song, you…
-Ploy.

325
00:26:36,385 --> 00:26:38,545
She probably knows where Piang is.

326
00:26:40,585 --> 00:26:42,345
Aren't we going after her?

327
00:26:42,945 --> 00:26:44,145
No.

328
00:26:44,225 --> 00:26:45,865
Let them sort it out themselves.

329
00:26:45,945 --> 00:26:47,665
If anything happens, she'll tell us.

330
00:26:56,745 --> 00:26:57,745
Hey.

331
00:26:58,705 --> 00:27:00,225
Are you really worried about Song?

332
00:27:03,825 --> 00:27:05,345
Yes.

333
00:27:05,425 --> 00:27:08,145
Song isn't just my coworker.

334
00:27:08,225 --> 00:27:10,465
She's like a real sister to me.

335
00:27:11,545 --> 00:27:13,225
I want to see her happy.

336
00:27:17,665 --> 00:27:19,985
But you can't worry
so much about your sister

337
00:27:20,785 --> 00:27:23,465
that you forget
your girlfriend is right here.

338
00:27:30,905 --> 00:27:32,265
Are you jealous?

339
00:27:34,745 --> 00:27:35,585
Make it up to me.

340
00:27:39,305 --> 00:27:40,785
How should I do that?

341
00:27:43,865 --> 00:27:45,305
Let's go to the room first.

342
00:27:50,905 --> 00:27:52,225
I'll go right now.

343
00:27:53,465 --> 00:27:54,505
Come on.

344
00:27:55,145 --> 00:27:56,305
-Let's go.
-Hey.

345
00:27:56,385 --> 00:27:57,865
-This way.
-Okay.

346
00:28:36,305 --> 00:28:38,145
<i>I don't care.</i>

347
00:28:38,225 --> 00:28:42,185
Even if I have to keep chasing her
until I'm exhausted, I'll do it.

348
00:28:42,705 --> 00:28:46,065
<i>Because love means everything to me.</i>

349
00:28:57,745 --> 00:28:59,065
<i>The problem,</i>

350
00:28:59,745 --> 00:29:02,905
is you refuse to move on from your past.

351
00:29:03,505 --> 00:29:06,505
<i>That's why Piang keeps chasing after you.</i>

352
00:29:06,585 --> 00:29:08,265
<i>And if the problem starts with you,</i>

353
00:29:08,865 --> 00:29:10,985
<i>then you're the one who has to fix it.</i>

354
00:30:10,025 --> 00:30:11,305
Song.

355
00:30:16,305 --> 00:30:18,185
Don't be afraid.

356
00:30:18,265 --> 00:30:19,665
I'm right here.

357
00:30:22,385 --> 00:30:23,425
Let's go.

358
00:30:24,185 --> 00:30:25,385
I'll help you cross the street.

359
00:30:28,665 --> 00:30:29,625
Stand up first.

360
00:30:30,425 --> 00:30:31,625
Wait for me a second.

361
00:30:51,585 --> 00:30:53,145
Hold on to my shirt.

362
00:31:38,985 --> 00:31:41,145
Thank you so much for helping me.

363
00:31:41,225 --> 00:31:44,305
What are you doing around here, anyway?

364
00:31:45,785 --> 00:31:48,145
I… just happened to be passing by.

365
00:31:50,985 --> 00:31:52,025
I see.

366
00:31:52,705 --> 00:31:55,985
Do you know
the boss is really worried about you?

367
00:31:57,505 --> 00:31:58,825
I know.

368
00:31:58,905 --> 00:32:01,065
But I've made up my mind,

369
00:32:01,145 --> 00:32:03,185
and I'm not changing it.

370
00:32:03,265 --> 00:32:05,945
Please tell Mudmee not to worry about me.

371
00:32:06,025 --> 00:32:08,785
Piangrawin isn't that easy to kill.

372
00:32:09,945 --> 00:32:12,385
That's good. In that case…

373
00:32:17,625 --> 00:32:18,825
Well…

374
00:32:18,905 --> 00:32:21,225
Would you like to go
upstairs and shower first?

375
00:32:21,825 --> 00:32:23,905
You'll get sick staying soaked like this.

376
00:32:25,225 --> 00:32:27,265
-I don't think I should…
-Go ahead.

377
00:32:27,345 --> 00:32:30,465
I promise I won't make you uncomfortable.

378
00:32:36,545 --> 00:32:37,385
Here's a towel.

379
00:32:42,105 --> 00:32:43,865
I think you should shower first.

380
00:32:44,585 --> 00:32:45,985
I'm fine.

381
00:32:46,065 --> 00:32:48,065
I'm the reason you got soaked.

382
00:32:48,145 --> 00:32:49,545
You should go first.

383
00:32:53,545 --> 00:32:54,825
Then let's shower together.

384
00:32:54,905 --> 00:32:56,265
Really?

385
00:32:56,865 --> 00:32:58,425
But…

386
00:32:58,505 --> 00:33:01,505
I have one condition.
Neither of us can turn around and look.

387
00:33:04,625 --> 00:33:05,865
Okay.

388
00:33:12,345 --> 00:33:13,665
It's strange.

389
00:33:14,465 --> 00:33:16,065
We've already seen everything,

390
00:33:16,145 --> 00:33:17,625
yet now we can't even lock eyes.

391
00:33:17,705 --> 00:33:20,665
So this is what it means
to be close yet distant.

392
00:33:21,945 --> 00:33:23,625
What nonsense are you talking about?

393
00:33:23,705 --> 00:33:25,385
The reason I don't want to look at you

394
00:33:25,465 --> 00:33:27,025
has nothing to do with that.

395
00:33:28,065 --> 00:33:29,385
Then what's the reason?

396
00:33:31,585 --> 00:33:33,825
You're afraid you
won't be able to resist me.

397
00:33:36,145 --> 00:33:37,345
Aren't you a clever girl?

398
00:33:39,425 --> 00:33:40,985
You called me a dog again.

399
00:33:41,065 --> 00:33:42,705
I might just turn around and bite you.

400
00:34:02,265 --> 00:34:03,465
Are you satisfied now?

401
00:34:04,145 --> 00:34:06,145
Satisfied about what?

402
00:34:06,225 --> 00:34:08,385
I never asked you to look at me.

403
00:34:08,465 --> 00:34:11,505
I was just talking to myself.

404
00:34:11,585 --> 00:34:14,784
You never stop teasing me.

405
00:34:15,744 --> 00:34:18,304
It's become a habit. Hard to fix.

406
00:34:20,665 --> 00:34:21,625
Oh.

407
00:34:21,705 --> 00:34:22,865
Song.

408
00:34:23,425 --> 00:34:25,505
When it thundered earlier,

409
00:34:25,585 --> 00:34:27,705
how did you know I was scared?

410
00:34:29,304 --> 00:34:31,185
Because what you're going through,

411
00:34:31,264 --> 00:34:32,744
I go through it too.

412
00:34:34,145 --> 00:34:35,985
You're afraid of thunder?

413
00:34:37,705 --> 00:34:38,625
No.

414
00:34:39,905 --> 00:34:41,344
Then what are you afraid of?

415
00:34:44,505 --> 00:34:45,744
I'm afraid of rooftops.

416
00:34:48,344 --> 00:34:49,665
What?

417
00:34:49,744 --> 00:34:51,625
People can be afraid of rooftops?

418
00:34:53,545 --> 00:34:55,465
Well, I am.

419
00:34:57,865 --> 00:35:01,105
Then if you ever
have to go to a rooftop again,

420
00:35:01,185 --> 00:35:02,505
don't go alone.

421
00:35:02,585 --> 00:35:03,785
Tell me first.

422
00:35:06,145 --> 00:35:07,905
I want to protect you

423
00:35:07,985 --> 00:35:09,985
the way you've protected me.

424
00:35:14,065 --> 00:35:15,785
I'll let you know if I do.

425
00:35:45,545 --> 00:35:46,745
I'm heading home.

426
00:35:50,625 --> 00:35:51,625
Okay.

427
00:35:52,305 --> 00:35:53,945
And if you're still coughing

428
00:35:54,025 --> 00:35:55,305
or start running a fever,

429
00:35:55,385 --> 00:35:57,425
go see a doctor right away.

430
00:35:57,505 --> 00:35:58,945
Don't leave it too long.

431
00:35:59,025 --> 00:36:00,105
It could get worse.

432
00:36:04,665 --> 00:36:06,385
You should go now.

433
00:36:07,225 --> 00:36:09,145
If you stay any longer,

434
00:36:09,785 --> 00:36:12,345
I might doing something
that makes you uncomfortable again.

435
00:36:16,985 --> 00:36:18,425
You should go back inside now.

436
00:36:20,825 --> 00:36:21,825
Okay.

437
00:36:48,145 --> 00:36:49,425
<i>Boss,</i>

438
00:36:49,505 --> 00:36:51,065
<i>I've found Piang.</i>

439
00:36:51,145 --> 00:36:52,265
<i>Don't worry.</i>

440
00:36:52,345 --> 00:36:54,145
<i>I'll take care of her.</i>

441
00:37:00,465 --> 00:37:01,745
Yes, Grandma?

442
00:37:07,145 --> 00:37:10,425
Why are you packing your clothes?

443
00:37:10,505 --> 00:37:13,625
I'm staying at a hotel for a few days.

444
00:37:16,145 --> 00:37:17,425
Well…

445
00:37:17,505 --> 00:37:20,025
That woman is having problems at home.

446
00:37:20,105 --> 00:37:21,945
So she's living on her own now.

447
00:37:22,025 --> 00:37:23,505
I'm worried about her.

448
00:37:23,585 --> 00:37:25,665
So I thought
I'd stay with her for a while.

449
00:37:28,465 --> 00:37:29,465
That's interesting.

450
00:37:29,545 --> 00:37:31,985
I met a woman yesterday too,

451
00:37:32,065 --> 00:37:35,265
and she was having
family problems as well.

452
00:37:38,385 --> 00:37:39,585
What did you do?

453
00:37:39,665 --> 00:37:41,425
I helped her out.

454
00:37:41,505 --> 00:37:42,505
But then again,

455
00:37:42,585 --> 00:37:47,025
if her family
can't understand or accept her,

456
00:37:47,105 --> 00:37:50,025
there's only so much I can do.

457
00:37:53,065 --> 00:37:54,505
That's why

458
00:37:54,585 --> 00:37:58,025
I'm so lucky to have a grandma
who understands everything.

459
00:37:58,105 --> 00:37:59,625
Of course.

460
00:37:59,705 --> 00:38:02,025
That woman is lucky too.

461
00:38:02,105 --> 00:38:03,945
She's lucky to have you.

462
00:38:04,025 --> 00:38:06,185
Make sure you take good care of her.

463
00:38:06,265 --> 00:38:07,345
Most importantly,

464
00:38:07,425 --> 00:38:12,705
you need to take care of yourself too.

465
00:38:13,625 --> 00:38:14,785
Yes, Grandma.

466
00:38:18,585 --> 00:38:19,905
You're the sweetest.

467
00:39:47,025 --> 00:39:48,025
Song.

468
00:39:53,265 --> 00:39:56,705
Hey. Did you book a room near mine?

469
00:39:58,825 --> 00:39:59,865
Yes.

470
00:40:01,105 --> 00:40:02,905
Just look at the state you
were in yesterday.

471
00:40:03,705 --> 00:40:05,625
There was no way I could leave you alone.

472
00:40:07,025 --> 00:40:08,705
If something happened to you,

473
00:40:08,785 --> 00:40:10,905
Boss would be heartbroken.

474
00:40:12,425 --> 00:40:14,745
So where are you headed?

475
00:40:14,825 --> 00:40:17,785
To the convenience store.
I need to buy some clothes.

476
00:40:18,865 --> 00:40:21,065
I've been wearing
this outfit for three days.

477
00:40:24,185 --> 00:40:26,265
Then why don't you shop at a proper store?

478
00:40:27,025 --> 00:40:29,225
My grandma cut off my credit cards.

479
00:40:29,305 --> 00:40:31,185
The reason you found me
on the street yesterday

480
00:40:31,265 --> 00:40:34,385
was because I had to buy food
from a local eatery myself.

481
00:40:34,465 --> 00:40:38,265
I can't afford the comfortable life
I used to have anymore.

482
00:40:38,345 --> 00:40:41,265
In a few days, I'll probably
have to leave this place

483
00:40:41,345 --> 00:40:43,745
and find a cheap room to rent.

484
00:40:46,625 --> 00:40:49,625
As for clothes,
you don't need to buy new ones.

485
00:40:49,705 --> 00:40:50,945
You can wear mine for now.

486
00:40:53,105 --> 00:40:54,065
Really?

487
00:40:56,025 --> 00:40:58,945
And if there's anything you like,
just pick it yourself.

488
00:40:59,865 --> 00:41:01,385
You're so kind.

489
00:41:04,745 --> 00:41:06,305
But…

490
00:41:07,825 --> 00:41:08,825
What?

491
00:41:10,225 --> 00:41:13,545
As for my bras,
they'll be too big for you.

492
00:41:16,465 --> 00:41:18,065
Song.

493
00:41:21,425 --> 00:41:23,945
It's okay. I'll just go without it.

494
00:41:24,025 --> 00:41:26,425
Lots of people these days
go no bra, no underwear.

495
00:41:26,505 --> 00:41:28,945
-It's comfortable too.
-Are you crazy?

496
00:41:29,025 --> 00:41:30,545
People will see everything underneath.

497
00:41:31,305 --> 00:41:32,865
How about this?

498
00:41:32,945 --> 00:41:35,825
I'll buy you all new ones.
I'll pay for them.

499
00:41:45,625 --> 00:41:46,705
This one.

500
00:41:49,785 --> 00:41:52,185
This one's really sexy. A lace skirt.

501
00:41:55,505 --> 00:41:57,425
We need enough for seven days.

502
00:41:58,945 --> 00:41:59,905
Red.

503
00:42:00,425 --> 00:42:01,665
You can wear it on Christmas.

504
00:42:07,825 --> 00:42:09,305
This one's for temple visits.

505
00:42:09,385 --> 00:42:10,825
Very proper.

506
00:42:14,945 --> 00:42:15,865
This dress is so sexy.

507
00:42:16,465 --> 00:42:17,625
I like it.

508
00:42:20,785 --> 00:42:22,065
Do you want anything else?

509
00:42:33,705 --> 00:42:35,265
It's really sexy.

510
00:42:41,105 --> 00:42:42,145
This one.

511
00:42:42,865 --> 00:42:43,985
Give it to me. I'll put it away.

512
00:42:49,105 --> 00:42:50,585
There's a rainbow too.

513
00:42:55,745 --> 00:42:56,985
One for each day of the week.

514
00:42:59,545 --> 00:43:00,985
For someone like you.

515
00:43:01,065 --> 00:43:03,105
A training bra is plenty for you.

516
00:43:12,865 --> 00:43:15,065
Are you sure you're not missing anything?

517
00:43:15,865 --> 00:43:17,585
I'm sure.

518
00:43:17,665 --> 00:43:18,945
Then…

519
00:43:19,025 --> 00:43:22,585
If you need anything,
just knock on my door. I'll be around.

520
00:43:24,025 --> 00:43:25,305
You'll be around?

521
00:43:25,385 --> 00:43:27,145
Aren't you going to work?

522
00:43:27,745 --> 00:43:28,705
I took leave.

523
00:43:31,985 --> 00:43:34,265
A workaholic like you took leave?

524
00:43:52,145 --> 00:43:52,985
Song.

525
00:43:57,305 --> 00:43:59,465
Can I ask you something honestly?

526
00:43:59,545 --> 00:44:01,545
Why are you helping me?

527
00:44:02,385 --> 00:44:03,785
I'm just…

528
00:44:05,425 --> 00:44:06,825
doing it for my boss.

529
00:44:09,585 --> 00:44:10,585
I already told you.

530
00:44:11,345 --> 00:44:12,705
If anything happened to you,

531
00:44:12,785 --> 00:44:14,585
my boss would be devastated.

532
00:44:23,905 --> 00:44:25,305
Really?

533
00:44:29,065 --> 00:44:31,145
If I don't believe that,

534
00:44:31,225 --> 00:44:32,905
and choose to think instead

535
00:44:32,985 --> 00:44:35,345
that you're doing this
because you care about me,

536
00:44:35,985 --> 00:44:37,065
would that be okay?

537
00:44:38,985 --> 00:44:40,305
Why ask me?

538
00:44:40,385 --> 00:44:42,465
You've been doing that all along.

539
00:44:48,865 --> 00:44:50,145
I'm leaving.

540
00:45:46,785 --> 00:45:48,145
Song!

541
00:45:48,225 --> 00:45:50,225
Help me, Song!

542
00:45:51,065 --> 00:45:53,025
Please open the door.

543
00:45:53,825 --> 00:45:54,985
Song!

544
00:45:56,425 --> 00:45:58,545
Song, please open the door.

545
00:46:00,825 --> 00:46:01,705
What happened to you?

546
00:46:01,785 --> 00:46:02,905
A ghost scared me.

547
00:46:02,985 --> 00:46:04,305
Huh? A ghost?

548
00:46:07,265 --> 00:46:08,185
Where is it?

549
00:46:14,305 --> 00:46:15,185
Oh…

550
00:46:15,265 --> 00:46:16,665
<i>Oh dear.</i>

551
00:46:16,745 --> 00:46:18,465
<i>She's even more scared than I am.</i>

552
00:46:23,105 --> 00:46:24,465
Where is it?

553
00:46:24,545 --> 00:46:25,745
I'm really scared.

554
00:46:25,825 --> 00:46:27,705
Can I sleep with you tonight?

555
00:46:27,785 --> 00:46:30,425
I promise I'll just sleep.

556
00:46:30,505 --> 00:46:33,945
If you don't trust me,
I can sleep on the couch.

557
00:46:34,025 --> 00:46:35,865
It's fine. We'll share the bed.

558
00:46:57,625 --> 00:46:58,905
Ahh!

559
00:47:01,625 --> 00:47:02,745
What?

560
00:47:03,865 --> 00:47:05,345
Well…

561
00:47:05,425 --> 00:47:07,065
I saw my reflection in the mirror,

562
00:47:07,145 --> 00:47:08,705
and it startled me.

563
00:47:08,785 --> 00:47:10,585
I thought it was a ghost.

564
00:47:19,545 --> 00:47:21,745
You seem more scared of ghosts than I am.

565
00:47:22,345 --> 00:47:23,305
It's okay.

566
00:47:23,385 --> 00:47:24,865
We're together.

567
00:47:24,945 --> 00:47:27,385
One ghost can't beat two people.

568
00:47:38,865 --> 00:47:42,465
Have you thought about
what you're going to do next?

569
00:47:46,345 --> 00:47:47,705
I don't know yet.

570
00:47:47,785 --> 00:47:50,705
But I definitely won't be
going home anytime soon.

571
00:47:52,185 --> 00:47:53,585
Then…

572
00:47:53,665 --> 00:47:56,225
you need to start
standing on your own feet.

573
00:47:59,145 --> 00:48:00,105
Why?

574
00:48:00,185 --> 00:48:02,665
You make it sound like you
won't be helping me anymore.

575
00:48:08,665 --> 00:48:10,505
You're an adult, Piangrawin.

576
00:48:11,545 --> 00:48:13,425
You need to understand

577
00:48:13,505 --> 00:48:15,865
that no one can be
there for someone forever.

578
00:48:17,065 --> 00:48:18,345
If something happens,

579
00:48:18,425 --> 00:48:20,905
we have to rely on ourselves.

580
00:48:22,025 --> 00:48:23,745
And once you can do that,

581
00:48:23,825 --> 00:48:25,705
the result is

582
00:48:25,785 --> 00:48:27,865
you'll love yourself more.

583
00:48:28,665 --> 00:48:30,145
When that day comes,

584
00:48:30,665 --> 00:48:32,705
even if no one loves you,

585
00:48:33,425 --> 00:48:34,985
you'll be okay.

586
00:48:44,225 --> 00:48:45,385
Is this

587
00:48:45,465 --> 00:48:47,865
another indirect rejection?

588
00:48:50,625 --> 00:48:51,785
No.

589
00:48:51,865 --> 00:48:53,265
I'm telling the truth.

590
00:48:58,865 --> 00:49:00,185
Okay.

591
00:49:01,985 --> 00:49:03,905
I know what I'm going to do next.

592
00:49:05,385 --> 00:49:08,265
I'm going to focus on my café for real.

593
00:49:12,145 --> 00:49:13,545
For now,

594
00:49:13,625 --> 00:49:15,985
stay and help me first.

595
00:49:17,145 --> 00:49:18,265
As for the future,

596
00:49:18,345 --> 00:49:21,545
whatever you decide…

597
00:49:21,625 --> 00:49:24,425
-I'll…
-Let's not talk about the future yet.

598
00:49:25,385 --> 00:49:27,345
Let's focus on making today count first.

599
00:49:27,945 --> 00:49:29,145
Okay?

600
00:49:32,465 --> 00:49:33,345
Okay.

601
00:49:35,545 --> 00:49:36,665
Let's get some sleep.

602
00:49:36,745 --> 00:49:38,185
It's really late.

603
00:50:00,265 --> 00:50:01,505
You little…

604
00:50:02,425 --> 00:50:03,465
Sleep.

605
00:50:32,185 --> 00:50:34,065
Excuse me.

606
00:50:36,625 --> 00:50:38,625
This one is our Shizuoka matcha.

607
00:50:38,705 --> 00:50:41,625
The flavor is well-balanced,
neither too bitter nor too sweet.

608
00:50:41,705 --> 00:50:42,985
It's easy to enjoy anytime.

609
00:50:43,065 --> 00:50:45,825
As for our signature drink,
the Little Cloud Matcha,

610
00:50:45,905 --> 00:50:47,385
please wait a moment.

611
00:50:47,465 --> 00:50:48,665
Thank you.

612
00:50:54,865 --> 00:50:56,425
Kate, is it almost ready?

613
00:50:58,225 --> 00:50:59,425
Piang.

614
00:51:00,225 --> 00:51:01,585
Mud.

615
00:51:15,065 --> 00:51:16,425
How have you been?

616
00:51:16,505 --> 00:51:18,505
I'm doing well.

617
00:51:18,585 --> 00:51:20,225
I miss you.

618
00:51:20,305 --> 00:51:21,905
Come back home with us.

619
00:51:21,985 --> 00:51:24,065
If you're still upset with Grandma,

620
00:51:24,145 --> 00:51:26,385
then just think of it
as coming back for me.

621
00:51:26,465 --> 00:51:28,025
Okay?

622
00:51:28,105 --> 00:51:29,105
No.

623
00:51:29,185 --> 00:51:31,065
I've made up my mind.

624
00:51:31,945 --> 00:51:33,345
You don't have to worry about me.

625
00:51:33,425 --> 00:51:34,665
I'll be fine on my own.

626
00:51:36,145 --> 00:51:37,305
<i>Ever since we were kids,</i>

627
00:51:37,385 --> 00:51:39,585
I've always been helping her out.

628
00:51:39,665 --> 00:51:42,465
I've never seen her solve
a problem by herself.

629
00:51:42,545 --> 00:51:43,985
Then…

630
00:51:44,065 --> 00:51:46,665
you should let her try this time.

631
00:51:46,745 --> 00:51:49,425
Because if she can do it now,

632
00:51:49,505 --> 00:51:50,905
from now on,

633
00:51:50,985 --> 00:51:53,385
you won't have to worry about her anymore.

634
00:51:55,265 --> 00:51:56,425
Okay.

635
00:51:57,025 --> 00:51:58,425
You've grown up.

636
00:51:59,945 --> 00:52:02,345
So what are you doing here?

637
00:52:03,985 --> 00:52:06,225
I'm taking responsibility
for what I created.

638
00:52:06,305 --> 00:52:07,785
Well…

639
00:52:07,865 --> 00:52:09,625
ever since I opened this café,

640
00:52:09,705 --> 00:52:12,465
I've barely been involved in running it.

641
00:52:12,545 --> 00:52:15,065
It's time I took it seriously.

642
00:52:15,745 --> 00:52:17,145
Besides,

643
00:52:17,665 --> 00:52:19,505
I need to make more money.

644
00:52:19,585 --> 00:52:21,385
I'm almost broke.

645
00:52:23,105 --> 00:52:25,185
Grandma cut off your
credit cards, didn't she?

646
00:52:28,185 --> 00:52:32,945
Yeah, Mud. I'll make our signature
matcha for you to try.

647
00:52:33,025 --> 00:52:34,825
Have a seat here first, Mud.

648
00:52:37,025 --> 00:52:39,625
Just wait until you taste my skills.

649
00:52:41,705 --> 00:52:43,185
Is it actually drinkable?

650
00:52:43,265 --> 00:52:45,865
Of course it is. I'm the one making it.

651
00:52:45,945 --> 00:52:48,025
What if I end up in the hospital?

652
00:52:57,745 --> 00:52:59,665
Thank you.

653
00:53:02,305 --> 00:53:05,425
Here it is, our signature drink.

654
00:53:05,505 --> 00:53:07,625
Enjoy.

655
00:53:08,385 --> 00:53:10,745
Hello. Please have a seat.

656
00:53:16,745 --> 00:53:20,945
Hello, everyone.
Today we're here at Zenzu Garden.

657
00:53:21,025 --> 00:53:25,465
And this is the café's signature drink.
It's the Little Cloud Matcha.

658
00:53:25,545 --> 00:53:27,545
I have to say,

659
00:53:27,625 --> 00:53:29,825
it's aromatic and well-balanced,

660
00:53:29,905 --> 00:53:31,345
and perfect for everyday drinking.

661
00:53:31,425 --> 00:53:33,025
Be sure to stop by and try it.

662
00:53:33,105 --> 00:53:34,705
At Zenzu Garden.

663
00:53:45,665 --> 00:53:47,265
Your drink is ready.

664
00:53:47,345 --> 00:53:48,785
Enjoy.

665
00:53:56,465 --> 00:53:58,265
-Your cake is here.
-Thank you.

666
00:53:58,345 --> 00:54:00,065
-Sorry for the wait.
-That's okay.

667
00:54:06,065 --> 00:54:07,225
Are you tired?

668
00:54:08,705 --> 00:54:09,785
Keep it up.

669
00:54:09,865 --> 00:54:10,705
Okay.

670
00:54:53,105 --> 00:54:54,545
Really?

671
00:54:54,625 --> 00:54:56,865
Piang is amazing.

672
00:54:56,945 --> 00:54:58,025
She is.

673
00:54:58,105 --> 00:55:00,425
Honestly, I never thought

674
00:55:00,505 --> 00:55:02,305
I'd see my little sister

675
00:55:02,385 --> 00:55:03,905
handling things on her own.

676
00:55:04,505 --> 00:55:05,785
It's all thanks to you.

677
00:55:06,545 --> 00:55:08,065
Thanks to me?

678
00:55:08,145 --> 00:55:09,105
Yes.

679
00:55:09,705 --> 00:55:13,105
At first, I almost stepped in to help her.

680
00:55:13,185 --> 00:55:14,225
But…

681
00:55:14,305 --> 00:55:15,585
what you said…

682
00:55:15,665 --> 00:55:17,505
kept coming back to me.

683
00:55:17,585 --> 00:55:18,745
It reminded me

684
00:55:18,825 --> 00:55:21,705
that I should let her deal
with her own problems.

685
00:55:25,545 --> 00:55:26,865
Thank you so much.

686
00:55:35,865 --> 00:55:37,345
Kwanrin.

687
00:55:39,665 --> 00:55:41,265
All this time,

688
00:55:43,185 --> 00:55:45,585
I've truly had strong feelings for you.

689
00:55:48,425 --> 00:55:51,585
Would you… mind

690
00:55:51,665 --> 00:55:54,105
if I asked you to be my girlfriend?

691
00:56:00,225 --> 00:56:01,705
Why are you laughing?

692
00:56:02,425 --> 00:56:04,865
Because this has to be

693
00:56:04,945 --> 00:56:09,825
the most formal confession
I've ever heard.

694
00:56:16,665 --> 00:56:18,905
Well, I've never had a girlfriend before.

695
00:56:19,705 --> 00:56:22,185
So, will you date me or not?

696
00:56:29,545 --> 00:56:30,625
But…

697
00:56:30,705 --> 00:56:33,905
you and I are very different.

698
00:56:35,425 --> 00:56:38,385
Aren't you worried about
what your grandmother will say?

699
00:56:40,145 --> 00:56:41,105
No.

700
00:56:41,985 --> 00:56:43,145
If Grandma objects,

701
00:56:43,225 --> 00:56:44,825
I'll do what Piang did.

702
00:56:45,745 --> 00:56:48,225
I'm ready to fight for our love.

703
00:56:52,185 --> 00:56:53,785
We're girlfriends now, okay?

704
00:58:36,185 --> 00:58:37,785
I'm home now.

705
00:58:41,265 --> 00:58:42,465
Good night.

706
00:58:48,505 --> 00:58:50,305
Who is this woman to you?

707
00:58:53,585 --> 00:58:55,985
-Did you have someone follow me?
-Yes.

708
00:58:56,585 --> 00:59:00,065
-Why would you do that?
-I wanted to know gave you the nerve

709
00:59:00,145 --> 00:59:01,385
to defy me.

710
00:59:02,545 --> 00:59:03,825
Let me tell you something.

711
00:59:03,905 --> 00:59:06,065
I've been watching you
and your sister all along.

712
00:59:06,145 --> 00:59:07,985
Whatever you two are up to, I know.

713
00:59:08,065 --> 00:59:09,265
So tell me,

714
00:59:09,785 --> 00:59:12,025
who is she?

715
00:59:18,065 --> 00:59:19,505
We're dating.

716
00:59:21,745 --> 00:59:22,945
What?

717
00:59:25,905 --> 00:59:27,225
And who is she?

718
00:59:27,305 --> 00:59:28,625
Where does she come from?

719
00:59:28,705 --> 00:59:31,465
She's just an ordinary woman, Grandma.

720
00:59:31,545 --> 00:59:34,545
She wasn't born into wealth
or any noble family.

721
00:59:34,625 --> 00:59:35,825
But she's a good person.

722
00:59:35,905 --> 00:59:38,585
-And for me, that's enough.
-You!

723
00:59:43,265 --> 00:59:44,905
If it were your younger sister,

724
00:59:46,145 --> 00:59:47,665
I could understand it.

725
00:59:47,745 --> 00:59:48,865
She's still young.

726
00:59:55,265 --> 00:59:57,385
But this is you, Mudmee.

727
00:59:59,665 --> 01:00:02,625
I'm truly disappointed in you.

728
01:01:55,145 --> 01:01:58,105
KWANRIN

729
01:02:04,905 --> 01:02:06,225
You're still on the phone?

730
01:02:07,465 --> 01:02:08,465
Yes.

731
01:02:11,385 --> 01:02:14,265
<i>You heard what Grandma</i>
<i>and I were talking about, right?</i>

732
01:02:16,505 --> 01:02:17,825
I'm sorry.

733
01:02:19,305 --> 01:02:20,945
<i>You don't have to apologize to me.</i>

734
01:02:23,865 --> 01:02:25,385
You did nothing wrong.

735
01:02:26,465 --> 01:02:28,385
I'm the one who's wrong.

736
01:02:29,345 --> 01:02:30,785
What do you mean?

737
01:02:43,945 --> 01:02:45,585
When I…

738
01:02:46,385 --> 01:02:47,825
agreed to date you,

739
01:02:48,345 --> 01:02:51,945
I think
I was being a little too idealistic.

740
01:02:52,665 --> 01:02:54,705
<i>I thought it would be fine</i>

741
01:02:55,465 --> 01:02:58,185
<i>even if things got complicated</i>
<i>between you and your grandmother.</i>

742
01:02:59,865 --> 01:03:02,865
But after hearing you talk
to her like that,

743
01:03:03,825 --> 01:03:05,585
I'm not okay with it.

744
01:03:07,145 --> 01:03:09,825
<i>I don't want you to have</i>
<i>problems because of me.</i>

745
01:03:14,785 --> 01:03:16,985
I think we shouldn't date anymore.

746
01:03:20,385 --> 01:03:21,585
No.

747
01:03:24,585 --> 01:03:28,425
We might be the couple

748
01:03:28,505 --> 01:03:29,785
that got together

749
01:03:29,865 --> 01:03:32,105
and broke up the fastest.

750
01:03:32,825 --> 01:03:34,585
<i>But trust me.</i>

751
01:03:35,265 --> 01:03:36,625
<i>This will be better for everyone.</i>

752
01:03:38,225 --> 01:03:39,425
No.

753
01:03:40,145 --> 01:03:41,825
It's only better for you.

754
01:03:41,905 --> 01:03:44,345
You're being very selfish right now.

755
01:06:12,905 --> 01:06:14,665
No ghosts have shown up for days.

756
01:06:16,425 --> 01:06:19,225
Why?
Do you want me to sleep with you again?

757
01:06:20,145 --> 01:06:22,345
No, I was just wondering.

758
01:06:28,745 --> 01:06:31,185
You look tired.

759
01:06:31,265 --> 01:06:32,705
You should get more rest.

760
01:06:33,745 --> 01:06:36,185
Okay. You too.

761
01:06:38,825 --> 01:06:40,265
Good night.

762
01:07:32,065 --> 01:07:33,825
SONG

763
01:07:34,465 --> 01:07:36,105
She's probably asleep already.

764
01:09:04,065 --> 01:09:05,705
<i>Please give me just two more weeks.</i>

765
01:09:05,785 --> 01:09:07,745
<i>Let me stay with Piang</i>

766
01:09:07,825 --> 01:09:10,745
<i>and take care of her until</i>
<i>I'm sure she's fully recovered.</i>

767
01:09:10,825 --> 01:09:12,504
Then I'll never show up
in front of her again.

768
01:09:12,584 --> 01:09:15,424
<i>You have to make her</i>
<i>fall in love with you within two weeks.</i>

769
01:09:15,504 --> 01:09:17,225
<i>If you can't,</i>

770
01:09:17,305 --> 01:09:20,464
<i>then you must accept reality</i>
<i>and give up on her.</i>

771
01:09:20,544 --> 01:09:21,945
So what did Song say?

772
01:09:22,025 --> 01:09:23,265
She was acting strange.

773
01:09:23,345 --> 01:09:26,705
<i>Like she was counting down</i>
<i>the time she had left with her.</i>

774
01:09:26,785 --> 01:09:28,464
<i>During all this time,</i>

775
01:09:28,544 --> 01:09:30,544
<i>that we've spent together,</i>

776
01:09:30,625 --> 01:09:32,584
<i>have you ever loved me?</i>

